{"id": "EUVD-2026-86101", "enisaUuid": "0f1175c0-87fd-387b-bc3a-c5e49332c8cc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngenirq/proc: Size interrupt directory names for 10-digit interrupt numbers\n\n/proc/irq/<n>/ directory names are built in `char name[10]` buffers\nwith `sprintf(name, \"%u\", irq)`.\n\nTen-digit IRQ numbers already need 11 bytes including the trailing NUL, and\ncurrent sparse-IRQ configurations allow interrupt numbers in that range.\n\nSize the temporary name buffer for the current decimal form and switch\nto bounded formatting when creating or removing the proc entry.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:04:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a8adf64fe7fd5d7c476769a043ee56eda7b775ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/488bcd7fd3e9a2ad647b71b505a269fdb28753c4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d4b22fbae70037299e96539c330e4a1054b28a91", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c2c7983c93f5d86962318be7e7298f1bc3feb1a6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7j5w-cr4g-jjc9", "CVE-2026-97503"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f0f22a4-ddc6-3eb2-8602-cade8e24f7e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "721255b9826bd11c7a38b585905fc2dd0fb94e52 <d4b22fbae70037299e96539c330e4a1054b28a91"}, {"id": "45a85124-f085-3f2e-9521-9f90044b1a02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "4dc6f1c8-bb2d-31e0-af7b-e8fefea025b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "7a725ac3-9e06-3a6e-ab9a-b72da2dc4317", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "721255b9826bd11c7a38b585905fc2dd0fb94e52 <a8adf64fe7fd5d7c476769a043ee56eda7b775ce"}, {"id": "ac87d876-2876-36ba-bc7c-416cf1dfc4de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "721255b